text:
jess: FYI CI flagged that our docs examples assume whole-page retries for streaming+pagination. gateway now supports resume tokens inside a page so snippets need to show how to resume mid-page instead of re-requesting everything. we should update py/ts/go samples and add a short compatibility note.
sofía: ugh, that explains the flakiness we saw in e2e. i can take the TS sample. will show async iterator + resume hook and a small helper for bounded retries.
tom: i'll do Go. want to show ResumeToken in the request object and an example backoff policy with jitter.
eli: i'll handle Python and the docs blurb (semantics + recommended backoff defaults). also add a note to RELEASE_NOTES about behavior change.
jess: great. minimal TS draft sofía put together (please convert to the SDK surface we publish):
```ts
// iterator that can be resumed using server-provided token
const iter = client.streamPaginate('/v1/resumable')
try {
  for await (const page of iter) {
    for (const chunk of page.chunks) {
      process.stdout.write(chunk.text)
    }
    const token = page.headers['x-resume-token'] as string | undefined
    if (token) {
      // record token and optionally resume on next iteration
      iter.resume(token)
    }
  }
} catch (err) {
  // transient error -> attempt bounded resume using last token
}
```
tom: Go pseudo-snippet: show explicit loop and backoff
```go
req := &client.PaginateRequest{Path: "/v1/resumable"}
backoff := NewBackoff(200*time.Millisecond, 3*time.Second, true)
for {
  resp, err := client.StreamPaginate(ctx, req)
  if err != nil {
    wait := backoff.Next()
    time.Sleep(wait)
    continue
  }
  io.Copy(os.Stdout, resp.Body)
  tok := resp.Header.Get("X-Resume-Token")
  if tok == "" { break }
  req.ResumeToken = tok
}
```
eli: Python: use a small helper to track resume_token and do jittered sleeps
```python
client = RedwoodClient()
resume = None
while True:
    resp = client.stream_paginate('/v1/resumable', resume_token=resume)
    for p in resp.pages():
        for c in p.chunks:
            print(c.text, end='')
    resume = resp.headers.get('x-resume-token')
    if not resume:
        break
    sleep(jittered_backoff())
```
jess: docs blurb suggestion (short): "Servers may truncate long streams under load; when responses include X-Resume-Token clients should attempt bounded retries using that token to resume within the same logical page. Avoid naive re-fetch of the entire page; prefer server-provided resume tokens and an idempotent cursor. Recommended backoff: base=200ms, max=3s, attempts=5, jitter=true."
sofía: i'll also add a tiny note in the TS snippet about detecting truncation (502 + header) and when to bail.
tom: i'll add a quick unit test in docs-ci that lints for 'x-resume-token' presence in code blocks to ensure we don't forget.
